  "hypothesis": "Reciprocity can remove valid geometric constraints, or only points that would already fail later native gates. Partition actual valid residual information at matched archived poses to distinguish these effects; no candidate rule is proposed.",
  "scope": "All inherited31 endpoints and all18 full native terminal histories rerun exactly. Passive queries at every joint/refinement iteration of modes6/7 (unfiltered100) and14/15 (fixed-reference reciprocal100). All other native observations remain complete exact controls, including16/17 duplicates. No endpoint or arm winner selection.",
  "intervention": "A diagnostic-only source transform evaluates the unchanged native query after each actual class reduction with reciprocity temporarily disabled under exception-safe scope. Private scratch, unchanged pose, same facade mask and field. A separate original double-coordinate reciprocal test partitions valid rows. No passive value enters optimization, prior, stopping, prediction, mapping or consensus. Normal solver then continues unchanged.",
  "observation": "Every source row retains native full forward neighbour indices, native validity and reciprocal keep decision. All/kept/removed count, H, g and Huber cost are retained per class at each fixed pose. Extra feature records preserve all geometry/reflector coordinates, row/cluster and intensity. Invalid rejected rows are explicitly counted separately from lost valid residuals.",
  "verification": "Independent float-coordinate forward ranking, full line/plane gates, original-neighbour PCA, original cubic field/derivatives, double-coordinate reciprocity, Huber/Jacobians, H/g/cost and additive partition reconstruct. Actual all or kept class equations plus unchanged recorded prior must match every actual selected native solver system/count. Every complete inherited stdout byte must equal the committed parent, including all558 outcomes and all old masks/profiles/features.",
